        "original_id": "4b4147d9-bcfa-5ba1-bfb7-ddee7ae6e54d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Britney Spears, Nicole Morier, Selena Gomez, Henry Walter, Patrick Leonard\n- Songs: \"Rock Me In\", \"Whiplash\", the other co-written song, the Henry Walter song\n- Topics: Latin pop influence, songwriting, co-writing, co-production, inspiration\n\nFacts:\n- Britney Spears and Nicole Morier wrote the songs \"Rock Me In\" and \"Whiplash\".\n- \"Whiplash\" was recorded by Selena Gomez & the Scene.\n- Britney Spears and Nicole Morier also wrote one other song together.\n- That other Britney Spears and Nicole Morier song has a Latin pop influence.\n- The Latin pop influence of that other song was described as similar to a song by Henry Walter.\n- San Pedro Town was said to be the inspiration for the Henry Walter song.\n- The Henry Walter song was co-written and co-produced by Britney Spears and Patrick Leonard.",
