        "original_id": "2d047164-7a3e-5070-a690-34dc3d1ba401",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Songs: Mmm Papi, La Isla Bonita, Whiplash, Rock Me In\n- People: Madonna, Patrick Leonard, Bruce Gaitsch, Selena Gomez & the Scene\n- Albums: True Blue\n- Places: San Pedro Town\n- Topics: Latin pop influence, songwriting, inspiration\n\nFacts:\n- In 1984, San Pedro Town was granted town status.\n- In 1986, Madonna released \"La Isla Bonita\" on her third studio album \"True Blue\".\n- Madonna and Patrick Leonard co-wrote and co-produced \"La Isla Bonita\", and Bruce Gaitsch contributed additional songwriting.\n- San Pedro Town was sometimes said to have inspired \"La Isla Bonita\", which opens with the line \"last night I dreamt of San Pedro\".\n- \"La Isla Bonita\" has been described as similar in style to the Latin pop influence noted in \"Mmm Papi\".\n- The same writers worked together on \"Mmm Papi\", \"Rock Me In\", and \"Whiplash\".",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "f4f279e7-50ac-5344-be19-ccef1233520f",
        "text": "Page: Mmm Papi. Sentence: \"Mmm Papi\" is noted for having a Latin pop influence, similar to Madonna's \"La Isla Bonita\" (1987).\nPage: La Isla Bonita. Sentence: \"La Isla Bonita\" (English: The Beautiful Island ) is a song by American singer Madonna from her third studio album \"True Blue\" (1986).\nPage: La Isla Bonita. Sentence: She and Patrick Leonard co-wrote and co-produced the song, and Bruce Gaitsch provided additional songwriting.\nPage: Whiplash (Selena Gomez &amp; the Scene song). Sentence: Together, they wrote \"Mmm Papi\", \"Rock Me In\" and \"Whiplash\".\nPage: San Pedro Town. Sentence: The once sleepy fishing village was granted the status of a town in 1984 and was sometimes said to be the inspiration for the song \"La Isla Bonita\" (which begins with the line \"last night I dreamt of San Pedro\"), written by Madonna, Patrick Leonard and Bruce Gaitsch.",
